  "fingerprint": "9cb70562a912db4b6bc263530af5250b6d23cf2393c2cc8508af965a582ec521",
  "definition": {
    "id": "ACT-SPEAK",
    "instanceId": "EX-CORE-U5-10-P01-speak",
    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "Choosing what fits · 1 · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the shopping vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U5-10. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare quantity, suitability and price before making a purchase.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-10-P01-speak-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-10-P01-speak-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "Choosing what fits · 1 · preparation 1: Present a supported viewpoint about the decision in this account. Refer to a concrete source detail, acknowledge a plausible alternative, and qualify what the evidence cannot establish.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "家附近的便利店也卖一些书。一天，我看到门口写着新书已经到了，就进去找自己预订的三本书。桌子上只有两本，我以为少了一本。\n\n店里的工作人员让我先看每本书上的数字。他说，这几本书一共有三本，第三本比较厚，放在桌子下面，不是还没有送到。\n\n我问他，为什么不把三本都放在一起。他让我看看桌子下面，第三本比较大，放在小桌子上容易掉下来。\n\n我们把三本书放在桌子上，一起检查书名和数字。每一本讲的内容都不同，拿到两本并不表示已经拿到全部内容。\n\n工作人员把书装进袋子，告诉我也可以邮寄。我想了想，决定自己带回去，因为住得很近，不需要再付运费。\n\n回家后，我先看了第三本的介绍，才从第一本读起。最厚的一本并不一定应该最先读，书的顺序要看内容，不能只看外观。",
